  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening - access to life-saving, quality, comprehensive, and confidential GBV services to conflict-affected women and girls in Buulobarde and Balad districts, Hirshabelle state.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $500,000 UNFPA project is to strengthen and scale up access to life-saving quality, confidential, safe, and timely GBV specialized services to women and girls. To that end, UNFPA will train health and social workers, provide small cash amounts to GBV survivors for accessing services, provide specialized case management for survivors as well as counselling. In total, UNFPA will reach 8,490 people, including 5,040 women and 2,310 girls.</narrative>
  </description>
